What does this program print?

public class Main {
    static String check(String price) {
        try {
            long p = Long.parseLong(price);
            return "ok " + p;
        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
            return "bad";
        } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
            return "illegal";
        } finally {
            System.out.print("[done] ");
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(check("12O000"));
        System.out.println(check("120000"));
    }
}

Res prints "open" when it is created and "close" when it is closed, and its close() always throws. What does this print?

public class Main {
    static class Res implements AutoCloseable {
        private final String name;

        Res(String name) {
            this.name = name;
            System.out.println("open " + name);
        }

        @Override
        public void close() {
            System.out.println("close " + name);
            throw new IllegalStateException(name);
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try (Res a = new Res("A"); Res b = new Res("B")) {
            System.out.println("body " + a.name + b.name);
            throw new RuntimeException("body failed");
        } catch (RuntimeException e) {
            System.out.println("caught " + e.getMessage() + ", suppressed " + e.getSuppressed().length);
        }
    }
}
